[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to improper handling of user authentication data, which can lead to a security risk known as Credential Stuffing. This vulnerability arises when the application does not implement adequate measures to prevent the reuse of credentials across different accounts or services. If a user’s email and password are not sufficiently validated or if the application lacks mechanisms to detect and mitigate repeated login attempts from the same credentials, it can allow attackers to exploit previously compromised credentials from other breaches. This can result in unauthorized access to user accounts, as attackers can gain entry using stolen credentials without facing any additional security checks or rate limiting.

